WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.357
- I said, "Dad, I remember
when we were growing up

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:04.960
"you said, 'I moved to
America with $12 in my pocket

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.187
"'and I really wanted to, you know,

00:00:07.187 --> 00:00:08.710
"'start a better life for everybody.'"

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:09.880
But I also know that I'm an actor

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.110
and I exaggerate everything.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.022
'Cause that's literally--

00:00:12.022 --> 00:00:13.915
- I don't know what you
are referring to, Kal.

00:00:13.915 --> 00:00:15.047
(audience laughs)

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:15.917
- So, I called him and I said,

00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:17.237
"I just want to make sure
I'm not exaggerating.

00:00:17.237 --> 00:00:19.190
"You moved to America with
$12 in your pocket, right?"

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.167
And he, very understated, he goes,

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.427
"I'm afraid you are exaggerating.

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:26.052
"When I moved to America,
I had $8 in my pocket."

00:00:26.052 --> 00:00:27.567
(audience laughs)
It's like (growls), man.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:31.357
- That's like the version of,
"I went uphill in the snow."

00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:33.870
- But the point is, yeah,
they worked incredibly hard.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.660
- There must've been some
incredible challenges.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.914
I can't even imagine that.

00:00:36.914 --> 00:00:38.320
- There were a lot of challenges.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.880
And I can tell you, they
did not move to America

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.854
for me to be an actor.

00:00:40.854 --> 00:00:42.080
(audience laughs)
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.450
Which I think was the
point of tell you that.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.070
But, they're so supportive now.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.710
I think part of it is,
for any parent really,

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.650
if you don't know that
that's an actual career.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.733
In a lot of places around the world,

00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:54.120
the arts are not a career,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.610
there's not a commercial
sector for the arts.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.520
It's scary, right?

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.530
You want your kids to have stability.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.730
The arts are not stable.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.970
Knock on wood and a
very fortunate few years

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.730
but you never know.
- You don't.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.340
And it's like this.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.173
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:07.173 --> 00:01:08.006
- At every level, right?

00:01:08.006 --> 00:01:09.720
- [Kelly] Yeah, agreed, agreed.

